privacy-review-au is an independent tool. It is not affiliated with, endorsed or
approved by the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner, any court or
tribunal, or the Commonwealth of Australia. It does not provide legal advice.

The bundled knowledge base (src/privacy_review_au/data/kb.json) contains quotations
from, and the text of, the following, used under their terms:

* Commonwealth legislation (Privacy Act 1988 and instruments, including the Privacy
  Regulations 2025, the Agencies APP Code 2017 and the TFN Rule 2015; Privacy and Other
  Legislation Amendment Act 2024; Digital ID Act 2024; Security of Critical Infrastructure
  Act 2018; Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979; Cyber Security Act 2024):
  sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation
  (https://www.legislation.gov.au), Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International.
  "Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation at 7 November 2026. For the latest
  information on Australian Government law please go to https://www.legislation.gov.au."

* OAIC determinations, media releases and guidance: Office of the Australian
  Information Commissioner website - www.oaic.gov.au, Creative Commons Attribution
  4.0 International. OAIC register metadata for 101 privacy determinations is included.

* Judgments of the Federal Court of Australia, reproduced in unaltered form as
  excerpts and acknowledged as decisions of the Court, via the Open Australian Legal
  Corpus (Isaacus, CC BY 4.0 as a collection; https://huggingface.co/datasets/isaacus/open-australian-legal-corpus).
  Analysis, headings and commentary in this repository are DeepCivic's, not the Court's.

* NSW material, via the Open Australian Legal Corpus: short quotations from the Privacy and
  Personal Information Protection Act 1998 (NSW) and from decisions of the NSW Civil and
  Administrative Tribunal (DMP, EQH, FQW, FMM, Insurance and Care NSW v FMM, Stalvies). These
  are cited only by analogy to the Commonwealth APPs. The decision texts are not redistributed.

* Administrative Review Tribunal (Bunnings Group Limited and Privacy Commissioner [2026]
  ARTA 130) and Federal Court ([2025] FCA 1224): the full texts were not retrieved. Quotations
  come from the OAIC's published statements on those decisions and are marked as secondary.

* High Court of Australia: short quotation only (Australian Broadcasting Corporation v
  Lenah Game Meats Pty Ltd [2001] HCA 63). The judgment text is not redistributed.

* The Commissioner's concise statement in Australian Information Commissioner v
  Medibank Private Limited (VID497/2024), as published by the OAIC. Its contents are
  allegations, not findings.

Research-time processing used Womblex (Apache-2.0, DeepCivic) and Isaacus kanon-2
models (enrichment and embeddings).
